step s3pk: EXPLAIN (COSTS OFF) UPDATE pt SET x = x + ps.w FROM ps WHERE ps.id = pt.k + 1 AND pt.id <= 40;
QUERY PLAN                                 
-------------------------------------------
Update on pt                               
  ->  Nested Loop                          
        ->  Index Scan using pt_pkey on pt 
              Index Cond: (id <= 40)       
        ->  Index Scan using ps_pkey on ps 
              Index Cond: (id = (pt.k + 1))
(6 rows)

step s3pf: EXPLAIN (COSTS OFF) UPDATE pt SET x = x + ps.id FROM ps WHERE pt.k = 0 AND ps.w = 0 AND ps.id < pt.id AND pt.id <= 40;
QUERY PLAN                                
------------------------------------------
Update on pt                              
  ->  Nested Loop                         
        Join Filter: (ps.id < pt.id)      
        ->  Index Scan using pt_pkey on pt
              Index Cond: (id <= 40)      
              Filter: (k = 0)             
        ->  Seq Scan on ps                
              Filter: (w = 0)             
(8 rows)

step s3pd: EXPLAIN (COSTS OFF) DELETE FROM pt USING ps WHERE ps.id = pt.k + 1 AND ps.w IN (1, 2) AND pt.id <= 40;
QUERY PLAN                                          
----------------------------------------------------
Delete on pt                                        
  ->  Nested Loop                                   
        ->  Index Scan using pt_pkey on pt          
              Index Cond: (id <= 40)                
        ->  Index Scan using ps_pkey on ps          
              Index Cond: (id = (pt.k + 1))         
              Filter: (w = ANY ('{1,2}'::integer[]))
(7 rows)

